## Definition of done

For `simple_paid_funnel`, use the dedicated subset definition of done. For coordinated full website + snapshot fulfillment, do not say complete unless all applicable criteria have direct evidence:

- approved retailer truth and no placeholders, cross-retailer values, or unresolved customer-facing claims;
- website generation, deterministic checks, desktop/mobile truth QA, D1/R2/runtime mapping, and rollback evidence;
- exact GHL portable object inventory resolved in the target by name/key, with no foreign IDs or contaminated values;
- all required workflows/actions/messages rebound and behaviorally tested in staging;
- calendar has verified users/team availability and every task has an approved assignee;
- compliance has one owner and suppresses every required outbound path;

- `lead_uuid` survives website→GHL→stage reporting without reminting;
- one approved lead proves D1, GHL, Sheet, and one deduplicated browser/server Meta `Lead` pair;
- approved GHL stage transitions prove the exact case-sensitive events and values;
- native/external AI configuration is either fully evidenced and tested or explicitly excluded;
- no temporary test code, number, trigger link, contact, or routing remains outside the approved cleanup policy;
- no required customer fact, target binding, runtime dependency, or behavioral claim remains `UNVERIFIED`, `NOT_ACCESSIBLE`, or `BLOCKED`; excluded items are explicitly marked not applicable with scope and reason;
- every unrun or blocked item is labeled, never converted to passed.

- for `flow: companion`, the treatment is delivered, not just the scope: every scene's cited blueprint or rules realized, the audio identity present (or the silence chosen and said), the open and close designed rather than defaulted;
- `npx hyperframes check` passes, including its built-in lint stage;
- design adherence is reviewed against `/hyperframes-creative` → `references/design-adherence.md` when a design spec exists;
- contrast findings are resolved;
- sub-composition snapshots are inspected when applicable;
