## Lock the fingerprint

Analyze every product reference and explicitly zoom into small details. Record:

- proportions, rim, corners, and cabinet/shell relationship;
- exact visible jets by seat/lounger, including ring shape/material/color;
- seating, footwell, filter/skimmer, shell color/pattern/texture/gloss;
- cabinet color, panel direction/texture, trim, seams, vents, fasteners, base, and badge;
- headrests and logos; control position/display/buttons; valves, lights, waterfall;
- steps, rails, cover, lifter, and other accessories;
- unknown details and supported camera sectors.

- imperfect eye/chest-height framing and slightly off-center composition;
- real mixed light or hard sun appropriate to the scene;
- ordinary mid-distance people, natural posture/clothes;
- believable home/showroom/event clutter;
- no cinematic grade, portrait bokeh, studio softbox, luxury catalog styling, or excessive polish.

Require rigid straight cabinet seams; restrained acrylic gloss; environment-matched reflections; water below the rim; physically caused ripples; one light direction; full ground contact and contact shadow; aligned steps/rails; and real full-size scale.

## Generate

Use `seedream_v5_pro` as primary model. Use 1K for 1000×1000 Meta feed batches and calibration. Use 2K when the placement, crop room, or micro-detail review needs it. Use the requested ratio; default to 1:1 only when no placement or dimensions are supplied.

For same-angle swaps, preserve the tub as unchanged foreground subject and edit environment, people, and lighting around it. When masking is available, protect shell, cabinet, controls, steps, rail, cover, and accessories.

## Run mandatory QC

Poll job status. Analyze the candidate side by side with every product reference and zoom into small details. PASS only if all comparable details match:

- proportions, rim, corners, visible jets, seating, footwell;
- shell/cabinet color, pattern, material, panels, seams, trim, and base;
- headrests, control, valves, lights, skimmer/filter, logos/badge;
- cover, steps, rails, and accessories;
- requested scene, angle, region, light, scale, perspective, contact shadow, water, reflections, anatomy;
- no invented text, branding, offer, sign, or proof.

Any product mismatch is FAIL. “Close enough” and “same type” never pass.

## Correct within caps

Retry a failed image once by appending only the named mismatch:

```text
CORRECTION: Previous output added two jets to the front-left seat and changed the cabinet vent. Match Product Reference 2 exactly: restore the original front-left jet pattern and the single rectangular vent in its exact position. Change nothing else.
```

Caps:

- one retry per failed output;
- at most four retries per ten-image batch;

